Comparison of the deceleration parameter $q(z)$ (top panels) and normalized expansion rate $E(z)=H(z)/H_0$ (bottom panels) according to the centered-scale hippopede simulations (a) and the same simulations but with stereographic projection (Eq. \ref{eq:projection_map}, $\alpha \simeq 0.283$, $\gamma_0 = \pi/3$) at fixed present time $t_0=3$ (b), both for several angles ($\chi=0^\circ$). Observational constraints shown in the upper subpanels include two present-day estimates $q_0$ from CC+Pantheon+SH0ES+BAO and FRB+SNe cosmography [Please include citation], together with two determinations of the transition redshift [Please include citation]. The shading area corresponds to GaPP of (model-independent) CC+Pantheon+ data [please complete very briefly, with references to methods that should be described in this manuscript.].}
